  "name": "Trapped in Darkness",
  "description": "You are trapped in the dark, and your memories lie scattered about. Each memory calls with a sound of its own: a music box, wind chimes, a piano note, a shimmer or a ticking clock. Walk onto a memory to take it back, and it plays a few notes of its own. Some memories are locked in glass cases: a case hums like crystal, knocks as you come near, and rings a bell when you are beside it. Then press Space to smash it. Creatures wait in the dark, breathing: one on the first level, one more on each level after, and never more than three. Each faces one way: come within three steps in front of one and it wakes, but beside or behind it you are safe. Smashing a case and stepping on broken glass are loud, and wake any creature within about ten steps. Broken glass stays where it fell, on every level after. A creature that wakes growls once, then charges straight at you for about ten seconds, running about three steps a second: you hear its footsteps coming, and where they come from. Keep moving away from them until they stop: then it rests again where it stands. If one catches you, the run is over. Find every memory on a level to reach the next. There is no clock, and you are not told which level is the last. Enter tells you how you are doing.",
